# Some of what is compared here is compared byte for byte, and a checkout
# that rewrites line endings would change those bytes: a golden would stop
# matching on every line of it, and a .luac would stop loading.  So the
# goldens are pinned to LF, and the compiled chunks are not text at all.
*.expected text eol=lf
testdata/luac/*.luac binary

# Four of the goldens are not text either -- they are what a case printed
# of a dumped chunk, or of a UTF-8 byte sequence -- and marking them text
# would have Git rewrite bytes that are part of the answer.
testdata/diff/14_utf8.*.expected binary
testdata/diff/37_dump.*.expected binary
testdata/diff/76_utf8str.*.expected binary
testdata/diff/78_new54.*.expected binary
